From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: created_shapes is filled only when EDEN_NX2_TC_LOG and debug lines ask for it (Lichii #428), on by default; EDEN_UP_TC_SHAPES_ALWAYS=1 is the old way

What: TextureCache::debug_stats started as true and was only set again inside the 600-frame report,
which runs only with EDEN_NX2_TC_LOG. So without EDEN_NX2_TC_LOG every new image added its shape
(format, type, levels, layers, width, height) to the map created_shapes, and the map was never
cleared. Only that report reads the map. Now the constructor sets debug_stats the way the report
would: EDEN_NX2_TC_LOG set and HW_GPU debug lines on. The periodic report is unchanged.

How much memory: the map is keyed by shape, not by image or address. It grows by one node per new
shape, about 64 bytes (libc++ map node of 32 bytes plus a 24-byte value, rounded by the heap).
A repeated shape costs no memory, only one map lookup per created image. So the growth per hour is
64 bytes times the new shapes seen in that hour. Upper bound, if every image were a new shape:
64 bytes per created image, so 1 MiB per 16,384 images. No log on file counts the shapes or the
images created per hour (searched; not checked on the console). Most likely well under 1 MiB per
hour: this is not big enough to explain a crash after 10-15 minutes by itself.

Switch: none needed to get the fix (it changes no picture and no log line without EDEN_NX2_TC_LOG).
EDEN_UP_TC_SHAPES_ALWAYS=1 (exact "1") fills the map again from the start, as before (a way back).
The switch is read once, when the texture cache is made.

Test: nothing to see in play. With EDEN_NX2_TC_LOG=1 and HW_GPU debug on, the "created Nx: format"
lines still come every 600 frames. A long run's memory line should not rise faster than before.

Origin and credit: Zortos, zortos293/Lichii 5637cf1c48 (#428, refs #401), "texture_cache: collect
debug statistics only when EDEN_NX2_TC_LOG asks for them"; same two lines, plus the way back.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index 8082a3f..4b83500 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -427,6 +427,17 @@ template <typename Runtime>
 template <class P>
 TextureCache<P>::TextureCache(Runtime& runtime_, Tegra::MaxwellDeviceMemoryManager& device_memory_)
     : runtime{runtime_}, device_memory{device_memory_} {
+    // 0745 (Lichii #428, Zortos): debug_stats used to start true and was only set again inside
+    // the EDEN_NX2_TC_LOG 600-frame report, so without EDEN_NX2_TC_LOG every new image shape went
+    // into created_shapes for the whole session and the map was never cleared. Now it starts as
+    // the report would set it. EDEN_UP_TC_SHAPES_ALWAYS=1 (exact "1") is the old way.
+    {
+        const char* const always = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_TC_SHAPES_ALWAYS");
+        debug_stats = (always != nullptr && always[0] == '1' && always[1] == '\0') ||
+                      (std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_TC_LOG") != nullptr &&
+                       Common::Log::IsLevelEnabled(Common::Log::Class::HW_GPU,
+                                                   Common::Log::Level::Debug));
+    }
     // Configure null sampler
     TSCEntry sampler_descriptor{};
     sampler_descriptor.min_filter.Assign(Tegra::Texture::TextureFilter::Linear);
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
index b005dd2..7bf577f 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
@@ -403,7 +403,8 @@ class TextureCache : public VideoCommon::ChannelSetupCaches<TextureCacheChannelI
     u64 keep_remade_deletes{}; ///< Kept images deleted so far (old pass, unmap, join)
     u64 scale_epoch{}; ///< InvalidateScale calls (EDEN_UP_L949_DESC_REPLAY)
     std::map<u64, std::pair<u32, GPUVAddr>> created_shapes;
-    bool debug_stats{true}; ///< Collect what only the debug statistics lines use
+    /// Collect what only the debug statistics lines use (0745: set in the constructor)
+    bool debug_stats{};
 
     static constexpr s64 DEFAULT_EXPECTED_MEMORY = 1_GiB + 125_MiB;
     static constexpr s64 DEFAULT_CRITICAL_MEMORY = 1_GiB + 625_MiB;
